pted only by a two-thirds majority of the Kongres.","106":"Decisions of the Kongres are taken by simple majority of the delegates present, unless the Constitution provides otherwise. The quorum is an absolute majority of the delegates.","106bis":"The right of legislative initiative belongs: to at least eight States, of which no more than half belong to the same constituent people (Article 1 bis).","106bis2":"Bills are tabled before the Kongres.","110":"Whenever the Constitution requires a majority in at least five of the seven national delegations, the delegations forming that majority must also together represent a majority of the citizens enrolled in the national registers, according to the latest annual count of the Confederal Chancellery (Article 115 bis).","111c":"Decisions of the Konfederalno Veće are taken collegially by consensus.","111":"When consensus cannot be reached, a decision requires the votes of at least four councillors whose peoples together represent a majority of the citizens enrolled in the national registers (Article 110), or the votes of at least five councillors. Where a seat is vacant, a majority of the members in office suffices; in the event of a tie, the serving president has the casting vote.","121":"An initiative for partial revision is submitted to the vote of the people and of the States. It is adopted if it obtains a double majority: a majority of voters at confederal level and a majority of the States (each State counting as one vote, determined by the popular vote within that State).","122":"One hundred and fifty thousand citizens, or twelve States of which no more than half belong to the same constituent people (Article 1 bis), may request that any confederal law passed by the Kongres be submitted to the vote of the people.","122e":"The act is submitted to the popular vote and is rejected if a majority of voters vote against it.","123bis":"A confederal law whose entry into force admits no delay may be declared urgent by the Kongres by an absolute majority of its members, with the approval of the Narodni Sabor by an absolute majority of its members and a simple majority in at least five of the seven national delegations. That approval replaces the alarm-bell procedure (Article 109 b). The law enters into force immediately. Its period of validity must be limited.","124m":"The confederal autonomous municipalities (Brčko, Mostar) vote with the confederal territories geographically closest to them, unless the law provides otherwise.","132b":"no State may, after equalisation, have tax resources per inhabitant below eighty-five per cent of the confederal average;","132c":"no contributing State may be deprived, by way of equalisation, of more than thirty per cent of the surplus of its fiscal capacity over the confederal average;","150":"The following provisions may be revised only with the approval of the Narodni Sabor by a two-thirds majority in plenary assembly and a majority within each of the seven national delegations:","n-art-123bis":"Urgent laws","n-art-150":"Entrenched guarantees","n-art-124":"Double majority","n-art-132":"Equalisation formula","n-art-110ter":"Conciliation","n-art-111":"Role, composition and decisions"},"new":["Skip to content","Open in the instrument","Fiscal capacity per inhabitant is taken as proportional to GDP per capita, the only indicator of Article 132 a published for every State.","Confederal average = 100","Assumptions of the instrument","The confederal average is that of the 52 States, weighted by population, before equalisation. Brčko and Mostar are not States.","Every contributor gives the same fraction of its surplus, never more than the ceiling. What the ceiling leaves uncovered falls to the Confederation, since the floor is guaranteed without reservation.","Result of the model: with a ceiling of {0}, the contributors fund {1} of what a floor of {2} requires.","Receives","Contributes","of the surplus","For","Abstention","Against","Passes","Fails","Suspended","Link copied","Copy link","The delegates of a State vote together, as their State is placed.","Every member is present; an abstention is not a vote cast.","Registers: population of the territorial States attached to each people, as no register count exists yet.","The voters of a State all vote as their State is placed; the weight is the resident population.","Brčko and Mostar vote with Sarajevo, the nearest confederal territory (Art. 124).","A member placed against votes the alarm motion.","The coalition is the set of States placed in favour; a confederal territory belongs to no people.","Consensus: no councillor against.","Share of the possible votes of the Kongres in which its delegates decide the outcome.","Exact count over every alignment of the other 53 constituencies. It also belongs to {0} of the minimal majorities of 126 seats ({1} of {2})."]}